var founderCopy = {
	headline: "Adam Thabo",
	paragraphs: [
		"Adam is a print specialist, designer, maker and educator. He brings over three decades of experience building museum exhibitions, immersive spaces and custom objects. He is the founder of Field Trip. His background in mechanical engineering at Imperial College London and Innovation Design Engineering at the Royal College of Art informs a practical approach to materials, structure and making.",
		"His work includes projects for Cooper Hewitt, Smithsonian Design Museum; the New Museum; the Jewish Museum; the Museum of the City of New York; the Noguchi Museum; the Museum of Jewish Heritage; and the Brooklyn Navy Yard Museum. Commercial projects include installations and brand experiences for Nike, Red Bull, Delta Air Lines, Hyatt Hotels, Nabisco, Sonos, TUMI and the 2012 US Olympic Swim Trials.",
		"Adam teaches in Interior Architecture at the Rhode Island School of Design (RISD) and Art and Professions at New York University (NYU), bringing the experience of the workshop into the studio and classroom.",
		"Through Elkan & Levinsohn, a. thabo connects his contemporary design practice with the firm established by his great-grandfather, Leopold Levinsohn, in 1909. Originally focused on graphic design and window display, the revived practice carries that history of visual communication and making forward. The name celebrates Leopold’s life and work."
	]
};
