var projectNarratives = {
	"women-who-rock": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication and installation for Women Who Rock: Vision, Passion, Power at the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Exhibition design by Pure + Applied.",
	"new-bamboo": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication for New Bamboo: Contemporary Japanese Masters at Japan Society. Exhibition design by Perry Hu.",
	"fox-studios-titanic": "a. thabo worked with Performance Structures on carpentry and light metal fabrication for The Titanic Experience at Fox Studios in Sydney. Designed by Technifex, the attraction included large motion bases and ship interiors.",
	"hunt-for-paradise": "a. thabo fabricated and installed Hunt for Paradise at Asia Society with South Side Design & Building. Designed by Perry Hu, the exhibition brought together carpets, manuscripts and decorative arts from Safavid Iran.",
	"central-governor": "field trip provided design, fabrication and installation for Saul Melman’s Central Governor at MoMA PS1.",
	"modigliani-beyond-the-myth": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication and installation for Modigliani: Beyond the Myth at The Jewish Museum. The 2004 exhibition brought together more than 100 paintings, drawings and sculptures, exploring the artist’s Italian Sephardic Jewish heritage and its influence on his work.",
	"coney-island-carousel-museum": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on the design, fabrication and installation of the interpretive exhibition for the B&B Carousell at Steeplechase Pavilion.",
	"touro-loeb-visitors-center": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication and installation for the Loeb Visitors Center. Exhibition design was by Charles Mack Design Ltd.",
	"bronx-science-holocaust-museum": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication and installation for Bronx Science’s Holocaust Museum and Study Center, with exhibit design by Robin Parkinson and architecture by Leo Blackman Architect.",
	"heliogram-series": "field trip provided engineering support for Saul Melman’s desert pinhole-camera system for the Heliogram Series.",
	"sacred-splendor": "field trip fabricated a custom textile display case for Sacred Splendor at The Jewish Museum. Exhibition design was by Leslie Gill Architect—Leslie Gill, Laura Lyon and Polina Stepanova—with graphics by Topos Graphics.",
	"core-nyc": "Field Trip provided industrial design engineering to assist with the implementation of AV components for New York at Its Core. The studio assisted fabricators South Side Design & Building with installation, particularly the map table and also the standing AV units. Studio Joseph designed the exhibition, Local Projects developed the experience and media, and Pentagram provided graphic design and identity.",
	"brooklyn-museum": "Field Trip provided design engineering for the illuminated Iris van Herpen garment display in Sculpting the Senses at the Brooklyn Museum. Original case by Chris Bellamy. Exhibition fabrication was by South Side Design & Building.",
	"cooper-hewitt": "Field Trip worked with South Side Design & Building on engineering, fabrication and installation for Ronald Rael’s Casa Desenterrada / Exhuming Home in Making Home at Cooper Hewitt. Johnston Marklee designed the exhibition, with graphic design by Office Ben Ganz.",
	"dia-beacon": "Field Trip worked with South Side Design & Building to fabricate tables and benches for Tehching Hsieh: Lifeworks 1978–1999 at Dia Beacon.",
	"china-institute": "Exhibition design by East China Normal University’s School of Design and Perry Hu, produced by Yongqiang Lin. Field Trip provided fabrication and installation with No.4 Studio.",
	"dream-machine": "Concept + Design by Emilie Baltz. Visualizations by Field Trip. Dream Machine is a multisensory installation combining sound, light and scent. Fabrication was by No.4 Studio, with sound design by Antfood and technology by Smooth Technology.",
	"electric-jukebox": "a. thabo worked with Odd Division on exhibition design for the Sonos and Janelle Monáe Electric Jukebox event.",
	"ascend": "For Delta at TED2016: Dream in Vancouver, Ascend invited visitors to climb through a responsive night sky of 6,000 lights, inspired by the airline’s Hangar research lab and the future of flying. Created with agency MKG and produced by Tool of NA, the installation brought together director Aramique, technical director Jeff Crouse / See Through Lab, animator Mau Morgo and composer and sound designer Gary Gunn. Field Trip collaborated with Odd Division on design and provided production design; Pink Sparrow fabricated and installed the project for MKG.",
	"bldg-92": "South Side Design & Building was selected to manage the complete production of the new museum at BLDG 92, Brooklyn Navy Yard. a. thabo worked as project lead and manager for over 18 months, coordinating graphic design services and assisting with all shop drawings for the museum’s exhibits. EAT (Exhibition Art & Technology) provided exhibition and graphic design, with exhibition designer Robin Parkinson and graphic design assistance by Stephanie Chen. The Brooklyn Navy Yard team included Daniella Romano, Aileen Chumard and Elliot S. Matz.",
	"on-becoming-an-artist": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on exhibition design for On Becoming an Artist: Isamu Noguchi and His Contemporaries, 1922–1960 at The Noguchi Museum. Agency: Pure + Applied.",
	"beat-repeat": "a. thabo worked with Odd Division on exhibition design and installation for Beat : Repeat at Red Bull Studios, presenting Joe Mansfield’s drum-machine collection with interactive media by Red Paper Heart. Red Paper Heart’s team included creative director Zander Brimijoin, technology director Daniel Scheibel, senior producer Lisa Walters, developer Charlie Whitney and designer Pedro Piccinini. Odd Division collaborators included Aramique Krauthamer and Nathalie Salazar, with a. thabo on installation.",
	"holocaust-by-bullets": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on exhibition design, fabrication and installation for the Museum of Jewish Heritage presentation of Holocaust by Bullets. The original exhibition was created by Mémorial de la Shoah in Paris.",
	"2012-us-olympics": "a. thabo worked with South Side on exhibition design and visitor experience for Speedo at the 2012 U.S. Olympic Team Trials—Swimming in Omaha. Interaction and graphic design were by Syrup.",
	"nike-free-hyperfeel": "a. thabo worked with Odd Division on industrial design for The Art + Science of Feeling for Nike Free Hyperfeel. South Side Design & Building fabricated and installed the project.",
	"wheat-thins-popped": "a. thabo worked with Odd Division on industrial design for Wheat Thins Popped, an interactive Times Square installation directed by Aramique through Tool.",
	"heart-bot": "a. thabo worked with Odd Division on industrial design for Heart Bot for Intel / SMS Audio, with direction by Aramique, technical direction by Jeff Crouse, engineering by Ranjit Bhatnagar and Matt Mets, and fabrication by South Side Design & Building.",
	"best-of-all-possible-worlds": "a. thabo provided fabrication and installation assistance for Saul Melman’s Best of All Possible Worlds, with South Side Design & Building. The artist’s making-of account credits a. thabo and Ani Weinstein as assistants. The installation was also presented at deCordova Sculpture Park and Museum in Lincoln, Massachusetts, in 2018.",
	"hyatt-photo-booth": "a. thabo provided design engineering and installation for Hyatt’s Mechanical Photo Booth, designed by Red Paper Heart and developed with Rokkan.",
	"tumi": "Field Trip provided exhibition design for TUMI’s 2017 Tribeca Film Festival environment, fabricated by South Side Design & Building. The viewing dome presented films from The Perfect Journey campaign, with dome concept by THEORIZ and campaign work by EP+Co.",
	"jadu-beta": "a. thabo provided engineering, fabrication and installation for Saul Melman’s Jadu Beta, an inflatable installation in Nevada’s Black Rock Desert. Wolf + Lamb created its eight-channel sound environment.",
	"m-is-for-museum": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on exhibit fabrication and installation for M Is for Museum at Carnegie Museum of Natural History. Wall-to-Wall Studios developed the exhibition’s branding and promotional campaign.",
	"david-bowie-residence": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication and installation of roof-terrace decking and furniture for David Bowie’s New York residence.",
	"klaus-biesenbach-residence": "field trip provided fabrication and installation for the Klaus Biesenbach residence.",
	"adam-fuss": "a. thabo worked as studio assistant to Adam Fuss in 2002–2003, during the year leading up to the artist’s exhibition of new work at Cheim & Read in New York (16 October–15 November 2003). His work included large-scale photograms, printmaking and installation. He also facilitated the collaboration between Fuss and Paul Taylor at Renaissance Press to create a dress photogravure.",
	"katrin-sigurdardottir": "a. thabo worked with South Side Design & Building on fabrication and installation for Katrín Sigurðardóttir’s Stage 2005/2012 at Art in General.",
	"intel-unknown": "field trip provided design for the Intel / Opening Ceremony product display."
};
